      'Turn-flow example: 1. **Deal**: Four cards each. 2. **Tricks**: Play four tricks; players must follow suit if possible, otherwise may play any card. Highest card of led suit wins and leads next trick. 3. **Knocking**: After players have viewed cards, and at any time during the hand, a player may knock to raise stake by one. 4. **Responses**: Other players choose to stay in or fold; folded players lose current stake and stop participating in the hand. 5. **Result**: Winner of trick four avoids hand loss; other staying players lose according to total stake.',
      'Scoring example: Penalty-life system where baseline loss is 1 life and each knock increases effective stake by 1. In standard round play, game ends when a player reaches 10 lives and loses the rubber; elimination variants continue until one player remains..',
